# Click something by colour instead of by coordinates - the usual way to hit a
# button you cannot predict the position of.
#
# Replace RRGGBB with the colour you are hunting for: run the app, hover the
# target, read the value under "cursor x,y" in the preview caption, or use
# `pixel x y` to print the colour at a spot.
#
# Always dry-run first:  hawk.exe --dry-run --file examples\find-and-click.hawk

shot before-look.png

# find <RRGGBB> <tolerance> <move|click|double>
try find 1E78FF 20 move
try find 1E78FF 20 double

verifypixel 5 5 000000 0

log Nothing found? Widen the tolerance or pick another colour with `pixel x y`
